From 41ac0de2b2565914748adb06ae88dc7277a5cd81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 06:50:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] settings, windowing/gbm/drm: what the modes read again
 retired goes once it cannot be read

When the display comes with other modes (CWinSystemGbm::RefreshModes()), the list of resolutions
before (CDisplaySettings::ReplaceCustomResolutions()) and what was read of the connector before
(CDRMConnector::Adopt(), and Refresh()) are kept, because other code may still point into them: a
reference that GetResolutionInfo() gave, read for the time of a call by any thread; a mode of the
connector, looked up and read in one function; and the selected mode of CDRMUtils, which stays a
mode of the read it was selected in until another mode is selected. They were kept until Kodi
ended, a few KB each time, with no bound.

utils/RetiredKept.h says how long: a retired list or read goes only when it is older than the 16
newest, and was retired a minute ago or more, and, for a read of the connector, when the selected
mode is not one of its modes. CDisplaySettings keeps when each list was replaced and lets go of what
can go at each replacement; CDRMConnector keeps when each read was replaced, and
CDRMConnector::ForgetBefore() lets go of what can go, called by CDRMUtils::SetMode() and
TakeConnectorModes(), which hold the selected mode (the one before and the one after the call). The
modes are made again only after a hot-plug event of the display and 3 s without one, while nothing
plays and no dialog is open (ModeListRefresh.h): a reference still read after sixteen of those and a
minute is not one of a call. Nothing else stores a pointer into them (no member holds a
RESOLUTION_INFO reference or pointer; OutputMove holds its mode by value). Replace() of
ResolutionListReplace.h does not change.

Checked on the host, AddressSanitizer and UBSan: RetiredKept.h with ResolutionListReplace.h on a
clock of the test (a reference into a list read until the list goes, never before 16 lists after it
and a minute; every 3 s at most 20 lists kept, every 100 ms 600, every 2 minutes 16); CDRMConnector
with a libdrm made of a script (a minute after 40 reads, all but the 16 newest and the selected
mode's go, and the selected mode is still read; on the tree before, none goes); SetMode(),
TakeConnectorModes() and ReplaceCustomResolutions() as the tree has them; and the test of
ResolutionListReplace.h, with AddressSanitizer and ThreadSanitizer, as before.
